\title{betanorm: Quantile and Beta-Mixture Microarray Normalization}
\description{
Provides quantile normalization that maps each sample onto a target distribution (requiring complete data), and beta-mixture quantile ('BMIQ') calibration of DNA methylation beta values to a gold-standard profile. Default expectation-maximization settings, including a small iteration cap, follow common legacy 'BMIQ' implementations for compatibility rather than as a recommended statistical default. Quantile normalization follows Bolstad, Irizarry, Astrand and Speed (2003) \doi{10.1093/bioinformatics/19.2.185} and beta-mixture quantile normalization follows Teschendorff, Marabita, Lechner, Bartlett, Tegner, Gomez-Cabrero and Beck (2013) \doi{10.1093/bioinformatics/bts680}.
}
